In article <1131@kl-cs.UUCP> jonathan@cs.keele.ac.uk (Jonathan Knight) writes:
>I find nethack to be something of a waste of time.  I've played 5
>or six games and have never seen level 2.  As fas as I'm concerned
>the game is no fun.


Well, you're just need practice at it, is the problem.  If you rush up to
a big, mean, hairy orc and start swingin' your wimpy dagger at it
and refuse to back off as he beats you to death, well sure it's not
going to be any fun.  You MUST keep in mind your abilities, what
resources you have (potions of healing, wands, ranged weapons, the
tip of your finger to write Elbereth with -- even your Minolta!)
and so on.  It's not as simple as just beating up monsters --
you have to be clever about how you handle a given situation.

I have gained some skill in playing older versions of nethack,
and got down to the 11th dlevel with a 9th level Tourist on one
of my first games at 3.0.  3 is quite a bit more challenging,
but that what makes it fun.
